### What evidence supports the characterization of Radio Quebec as a "conspiracy network"?
Answer: The search result from Conspiracy Watch provides extensive evidence supporting the characterization of Radio Quebec as a "conspiracy network." The source directly labels Alexis Cossette-Trudel as a "vidéaste complotiste québécois" (Quebec conspiracy theorist video creator) and details how his channel promoted numerous conspiracy theories including QAnon, Pizzagate, the "New World Order," Freemason plots, and various COVID-19 misinformation—including claims that the pandemic was premeditated, that governments deliberately inflated death statistics, and false accusations linking scientists like Charles Lieber to creating the virus. Cossette-Trudel also accused Prime Minister Justin Trudeau of involvement in a "vaste complot pédophile," promoted claims that elites "vénèrent Lucifer" and practice "satanic rituals," and spread skepticism about verified events like the killing of Qassem Soleimani. His YouTube channel was ultimately removed by YouTube for "repeatedly violating policies regarding misinformation" related to COVID-19, and he was reported to have encouraged supporters to create fake social media accounts to spread "conspiratorial and antivax content" in a covert manner. This pattern of promoting multiple, well-documented conspiracy theories constitutes strong evidence for characterizing Radio Quebec as a conspiracy network.

Source URL: https://www.conspiracywatch.info/notice/alexis-cossette-trudel

### Did Facebook take action to remove or ban content published by Radio Quebec?
Answer: Yes, Facebook took action to remove and ban content published by Radio Quebec. According to Radio Canada, Facebook Canada announced the closure of pages linked to the network, stating, "Nous fermons maintenant les pages, les groupes et les comptes Instagram qui représentent QAnon, y compris Radio-Québec." The article also notes that prior to this, Facebook had already acted to limit Radio Quebec's influence, including removing monetization capabilities and restricting its appearance in search results.

Source URL: https://ici.radio-canada.ca/nouvelle/1739379/facebook-radio-quebec-qanon-conspiration

### What specific action did Facebook take against Radio Quebec's content (e.g., page removal, account suspension, content demotion)?
