## Final Judgement
The key findings from the evidence confirm that Facebook Canada officially announced the closure of pages, groups, and Instagram accounts representing the QAnon movement, explicitly including "Radio-Québec." This action was taken on October 7, 2020, coinciding with the claim date, and followed a policy decision by Facebook to limit QAnon content. The source provides a direct quote from Facebook Canada confirming the removal.

The evidence is clear and comprehensive, with no contradictory information. No further investigation is required to finalize the fact-check.

Based on the recorded evidence, the claim that Facebook banned the content of the conspiracy network Radio Quebec is directly confirmed by Facebook's own public statement and reported actions. Therefore, the claim is `supported`.

### Verdict: SUPPORTED

### Justification
The fact-check confirms that Facebook Canada officially announced on October 7, 2020, the closure of pages, groups, and Instagram accounts representing QAnon, explicitly including Radio-Québec, as part of a new policy to remove such content. This action, which included prior restrictions on monetization and search visibility, was [reported by CBC](https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/montreal/radio-qu%C3%A9bec-facebook-qanon-1.5753487) and [Radio Canada](https://ici.radio-canada.ca/nouvelle/1739379/facebook-radio-quebec-qanon-conspiration) with a direct quote from Facebook Canada confirming the removal. The evidence characterizes Radio-Québec as a conspiracy network promoting QAnon and other misinformation, and the claim is fully supported by Facebook's own statement.